cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite this repository and its associated non-peer-reviewed public preprint using
  the metadata below. The preprint is publicly available on ResearchGate (see
  preferred-citation url). No journal, volume, issue, or Zenodo DOI has been assigned
  or confirmed yet.
title: "HATI-Madrid - Heat-Adaptive Tourism Opportunity Screening (Madrid pilot)"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pilot that screens urban tourism opportunities under extreme heat with a
  constraint-first, uncertainty-aware architecture, and tests whether the choice of thermal
  method (a simple operational proxy vs a physically based SOLWEIG/UTCI configuration)
  changes tourism-feasibility classifications and the surviving candidate set. Single-day,
  single-city pilot in central Madrid; no field validation of Tmrt/UTCI and no behavioural
  data.
type: software
authors:
